{# THE SCOPE CONTROL — the shell's, and the one control an organization-level
   page carries in its action row.

   A MODULE STATES NO SCOPE CONTROL OF ITS OWN. Every org-level surface the
   seam contributes gets this one, so "which slice am I looking at" is asked
   the same way on every page in the product and no module sheet restates it.

   IT IS A FORM WITH NO BUTTON, and that is deliberate: the control changes
   where you are looking, which is a navigation, so it submits on change with
   the script and submits on Enter without one. Nothing here needs JavaScript
   to work — `method="get"` and the page reloads at the new address.

   ONE PARAMETER, `?area=`, named once in Shell\Service\Scopes. A link from
   anywhere to "this page, that area" is a link anybody can write.

   PARAMETERS:
     scopes   list<Scope> — what this viewer may look at, the host's answer
     current  Scope       — the one the page is drawn at
     label    the control's own word; "Scope" unless a page has a better one #}
{% if scopes|length > 1 %}
    <form class="ov-ctl" method="get" data-controller="uhifadhi--shell-bundle--scope">
        <span class="k">{{ label|default('Scope') }}</span>
        <span class="fsel">
            <select class="fld" name="{{ constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\ShellBundle\\Service\\Scopes::PARAMETER') }}"
                    aria-label="{{ label|default('Scope') }}"
                    data-action="change->uhifadhi--shell-bundle--scope#go">
                {% for scope in scopes %}
                    <option value="{{ scope.areaUuid }}"{{ scope.is(current) ? ' selected' }}>{{ scope.label }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>
        </span>
    </form>
{% endif %}
